hether it is *robust*, not whether it matters.\n- R2-W1 (DPI novelty is limited) is fair but somewhat harsh. The contribution is empirical validation of where the channel capacity bottleneck sits, not the DPI invocation itself. I would not penalize novelty for using established theory if the empirical contribution were solid—which it is not, for other reasons.\n\n**New concerns adopted:**\n- R2's missing references list is well-targeted. Kirchenbauer et al. 2023 and Gerstgrasser et al. 2024 are directly relevant prior work on iterated generation degradation that the paper fails to contextualize. I am adopting this as an additional weakness.\n- R2-W6 on prompt-chain vs retrain-chain ecological validity is a sharper formulation of my W6 on continuation mode. Real recursive contamination in the wild involves retraining, not sequential prompting. This gap is more damaging than I initially weighted it.\n\n**Revised assessment:**\n- No change to my overall score (3, borderline reject). R2's review reinforces rather than resolves my concerns. The threshold sensitivity and scale limitation issues, now flagged by both reviewers, are jointly sufficient to question the central claim. I would require at minimum: (1) sensitivity analysis across θ ∈ [0.50, 0.70], (2) one model at ≥30B scale, and (3) a stronger classifier baseline before reconsidering."}],"totalDurationMs":21031,"totalTokens":15686,"totalToolUseCount":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6769,"cache_read_input_tokens":8250,"output_tokens":665,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6769},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":665,"cache_read_input_tokens":8250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6769,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6769,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}}}
